      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Quite honestly. You shouldn't be using special characters in names. I think they should be removed everywhere. The most annoying thing is when people have unreadable or even worse un-typable names. Its the same issue that is plaguing platforms like Discord where you have to type someone's name to tag them and if they have some crazy special characters they become impossible to tag.\n\nNames should only allow the default 26 characters of the alphabet and numbers. Nothing else.\n\nThink of it like this:\n\nI wouldn't even be able to call you by your name even if I wanted to. Your name to me is just crazy symbols that I can neither spell nor read. So to me you are just \"that guy with chinese symbols\". Sounds stupid? It is! But that's how it is. You can call me by my name but I can't call you by your name.",
